  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35734758",
      "title": "Sending a POST HTTP Request",
      "sourceHash": "cc51b922d1b991bfb31e60660ac4535fb9db353320e803037ab41c0c68e07d04",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.55,
          "end": 4.14,
          "en": "So how can we send requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.14,
          "end": 8.721,
          "en": "from inside our React application to a backend?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.721,
          "end": 12.69,
          "en": "Well, let's start with creating new posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.69,
          "end": 15.671,
          "en": "For that we got this new post component and there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.671,
          "end": 19.383,
          "en": "at the moment I have this submit handler where I",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.383,
          "end": 22.89,
          "en": "have the end call on add post and pass the collected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.89,
          "end": 27.15,
          "en": "post data to the parent component of new post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.15,
          "end": 30.51,
          "en": "In this case, that's the post list component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.51,
          "end": 32.82,
          "en": "There, I'm using the new post component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.82,
          "end": 36.48,
          "en": "and on add post we're executing this add post handler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.48,
          "end": 40.455,
          "en": "where at the moment we're updating this local post state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 40.455,
          "end": 44.34,
          "en": "Well, we definitely still want that local post state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 44.34,
          "end": 46.856,
          "en": "because we still want to render some posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.856,
          "end": 51.21,
          "en": "but we also wanna send that data to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 51.21,
          "end": 53.97,
          "en": "And in that backend code, just as a side note,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.97,
          "end": 55.71,
          "en": "this API route should be hit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.71,
          "end": 59.31,
          "en": "a post request should be sent to this path on the backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.31,
          "end": 61.17,
          "en": "and there this post will be stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.17,
          "end": 63.21,
          "en": "in a file in this post JSON file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.21,
          "end": 66.63,
          "en": "enriched with an extra pseudo unique ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.63,
          "end": 68.46000000000001,
          "en": "But that's just a side note.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.46000000000001,
          "end": 71.7,
          "en": "So that's the path to which a request should be sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.7,
          "end": 75,
          "en": "And to do that, we can use the fetch API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75,
          "end": 78.69,
          "en": "The fetch function is available in browsers out of the box.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.69,
          "end": 80.46000000000001,
          "en": "It's not a React feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.46000000000001,
          "end": 84.51,
          "en": "And fetch can be used to send HTTP requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.51,
          "end": 87.57,
          "en": "And unlike the name suggests you cannot just use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.57,
          "end": 90.51,
          "en": "to fetch data, but also to send data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.51,
          "end": 92.34,
          "en": "It's a bit confusing but that's what you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.34,
          "end": 94.233,
          "en": "can do with that fetch function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.31,
          "end": 98.55,
          "en": "Now fetch takes the url to which you wanna send the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.55,
          "end": 101.88,
          "en": "and in my case that's local host 8080, local host",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.88,
          "end": 104.22,
          "en": "because this backend runs locally on our machine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.22,
          "end": 107.07,
          "en": "and 8080 as mentioned is the port",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.07,
          "end": 109.32300000000001,
          "en": "on which we listed on this backend server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.37,
          "end": 114.93,
          "en": "So we send a request to this URL or to this domain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.93,
          "end": 117.78,
          "en": "And then there specifically, we wanna target the slash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.78,
          "end": 120.752,
          "en": "posts path here because as I just mentioned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.752,
          "end": 125.43,
          "en": "it's this slash posts path here where we expect a post",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.43,
          "end": 128.823,
          "en": "request if we wanna store a new post in this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.84,
          "end": 133.2,
          "en": "Therefore, we also have to configure this request because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.2,
          "end": 136.47,
          "en": "by default fetch sends a get request and we can now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.47,
          "end": 138.722,
          "en": "pass an object as a second argument to fetch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.722,
          "end": 142.17000000000002,
          "en": "to set the method to post, to turn this into a",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.17000000000002,
          "end": 145.59,
          "en": "post request and to then also add a body, so",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 145.59,
          "end": 148.713,
          "en": "the data that should be attached to this outgoing request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 149.57999999999998,
          "end": 152.07,
          "en": "And here the data I do wanna send is my post data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.07,
          "end": 154.59,
          "en": "of course, the data we're getting here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 154.59,
          "end": 157.23,
          "en": "but we have to convert this to JSON.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 157.23,
          "end": 159.81,
          "en": "So to the JSON format, which we can do with the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 159.81,
          "end": 163.023,
          "en": "built in JSON object and the stringify method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 164.04,
          "end": 167.16,
          "en": "With that, we turn that data into JSON, as we must do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 167.16,
          "end": 168.93,
          "en": "And then last, but not least we should add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 168.93,
          "end": 171.63,
          "en": "some headers to this outgoing request by setting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 171.63,
          "end": 173.73,
          "en": "an object on this header's property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 173.73,
          "end": 175.95,
          "en": "And here I want to add the content type header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 175.95,
          "end": 178.5,
          "en": "and set this to application JSON.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 178.5,
          "end": 180.72,
          "en": "And that's how we could send such a post request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 180.72,
          "end": 185.163,
          "en": "with our post data to the right path on this dummy backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 186.06,
          "end": 188.79,
          "en": "Now fetch will then send this request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 188.79,
          "end": 192.656,
          "en": "hit this API route here, this API resource",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 192.656,
          "end": 196.2,
          "en": "and then ultimately it will return a response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 196.2,
          "end": 198.288,
          "en": "Now for the moment, I'm not really interested",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 198.288,
          "end": 202.11,
          "en": "in the response here, and therefore we can just save this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 202.11,
          "end": 207.11,
          "en": "And if we do so and I add a new post test max",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 207.84,
          "end": 209.61,
          "en": "it still appears locally because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 209.61,
          "end": 211.98,
          "en": "I still update my posts as I did before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 211.98,
          "end": 214.59,
          "en": "But if we switch to the backend here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 214.59,
          "end": 216.6,
          "en": "we should see that in posts JSON",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 216.6,
          "end": 218.313,
          "en": "we also got the post here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 219.81,
          "end": 223.233,
          "en": "So it was indeed received on the backend and stored there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 224.22,
          "end": 226.66899999999998,
          "en": "And that's generally how we can send the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 226.66899999999998,
          "end": 229.71,
          "en": "from our front end to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 229.71,
          "end": 232.23,
          "en": "Nothing special about that here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 232.23,
          "end": 234.18,
          "en": "It's the standard fetch function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 234.18,
          "end": 236.35399999999998,
          "en": "and it does what we would expect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 236.35399999999998,
          "end": 239.79,
          "en": "But of course we now also wanna fetch data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 239.79,
          "end": 242.61,
          "en": "We wanna make sure that if we reload this page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 242.61,
          "end": 245.13,
          "en": "or if we visit it for the first time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 245.13,
          "end": 247.62,
          "en": "we fetch the available posts from the back end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 247.62,
          "end": 250.653,
          "en": "And here things become a bit more tricky.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}